From 532efb480d58e59854086cb3271093fcad054314 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Van Tran <trantoanvan@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:08:16 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(storage): allow the index database outside the vault

OBSIDIAN_DB_PATH (absolute path) places the index database, with its WAL and
shared-memory files, outside the vault so sync tools no longer copy it. The
parent directory is created on open. A database outside the default location
is refused when the vault recorded in it differs from the active vault.

With OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH set, --db now also selects an existing database that
records that vault; the selection is exported through OBSIDIAN_DB_PATH so the
daemon and every transport open the same file. status reports db_path.
Nothing changes when neither is used.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
